        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d765f101-5515-5983-8568-3f27f5badb51",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Claude Trichet, Mario Draghi, Silvio Berlusconi\n- Organizations: European Central Bank, Financial Stability Board, Bank of Italy, Italian government\n- Events: European banking crisis, ECB letter to Italy\n- Roles: President of the European Central Bank, Chairman of the Financial Stability Board, Governor of the Bank of Italy\n\nFacts:\n- From 2005 to 2011, Mario Draghi served as Governor of the Bank of Italy.\n- From 2009 to 2011, Mario Draghi served as Chairman of the Financial Stability Board.\n- On 5 August 2011, during the European banking crisis, Jean Claude Trichet and Mario Draghi wrote a secret letter to the Italian government led by Silvio Berlusconi urging economic measures to be implemented as soon as possible.\n- In November 2011, Mario Draghi became President of the European Central Bank.\n- Mario Draghi was born on 3 September 1947 and is an Italian economist.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
